the john wick franchise takes place in a  stylish reality that while captivating  doesn't always make total sense here are  a few questionable aspects of the john  wick movies that many fans choose to  ignore  how are there so many assassins in one  place at any given time new york in  particular appears to be infested with  them as the story of john wick continues  it becomes apparent that wick isn't the  only assassin around the continental  hotel for example is an entire boarding  facility dedicated to provide a safe  space for those in the business to relax  have a drink and restock on whatever  weapons and ammo they might need when  jon is declared excommunicado by winston  the owner of the new york continental at  the end of john wick chapter 2 every  single person who happens to be outside  during the public meeting turns out to  be part of the criminal underworld as  wick begins his hour-long head start  many of the people he runs past read the  excommunicado notification on their cell  phones and look at him with solemn  recognition it's a striking scene that  shows how relatively powerless wick is  when compared to the authority of the  all-seeing high table but don't think  about it too hard or it might lose some  of its movie magic why do we ignore this  plethora of murderous hit people or  congregating in the same public place it  does make sense that they'd all be near  the continental and that the various new  york mobs would have enforcers stationed  nearby but 100 of the people there it  doesn't make sense even in the world of  wick with this many assassins around the  underworld sees this being the  underworld at this point it's just the  world  in the shadowy black markets of the john  wick franchise the gold coin is the  currency of choice wick's stash of gold  buys him everything from a taxi ride for  his dog to corp's disposal medical  attention guns a new suit all of it  costs a single coin each and no one ever  refuses it as payments as explained by  sci-fi wire the coins aren't just about  payment but about a code that keeps  everyone working for the mythical  world's high table on the honor system  instead of representing a set amount of  money a coin represents a favor that can  be redeemed for anything else one might  need that is unless you're shopping at a  normal store like a normal person  assassins need to eat too after all we  know from the first film that viggo  tarasoff has plenty of cash alongside  his coins and that other mob bosses have  enough cash lying around that it needs  to be laundered additionally bounties  posted on the operator's board are  offered not in coins but in cold hard  cash what makes something worth paying  coins and not cash if coins are the  currency that buys loyalty and silence  why offer cash at all everyone has  regular money in this world the trouble  starts for germany's buying gas after  all but the exact nature of this  underground economy doesn't exactly add  up  in the scene where viggo tells joseph  exactly who and how dangerous john wick  is he refers to him as baba yaga as well  as the boogeyman or more accurately he  was the one you sent to kill the [ __ ]  the only problem is that john wick is  nothing like baba yaga at least not the  virgin from russian folklore according  to the legend baba yaga is an old witch  who eats children and lives in a house  that walks on chicken legs yes she and  wick are both russian but that's about  where the similarities end baba yaga is  a russian boogeyman used to scare  children into behaving but wick is  nothing like her if the fairy tales are  to be believed it's a cool nickname  though and sounds very intimidating  which is probably why wic fans are  willing to look past it one thing the  john wick franchise has plenty of is  mayhem while some of it occurs in dark  rooms and elaborate set pieces most of  it occurs in public spaces where most of  the people present are presumably  innocent bystanders drawing some of  those public fights bystanders scream  and scatter as soon as bullets start  flying in other cases though no one  seems to notice the violence taking  place right in front of them probably  the least plausible of these fights is  the final altercation between john wick  and cassian the bodyguard of giana the  woman john has been sent to assassinate  in john wick chapter 2. john and cassian  take shots at each other in a subway  station while everyone else continues to  go about their business seemingly  unaware that a firefight is going on  sure both men have silencers on their  guns but silencers don't really work  that way john and cassian's fight being  ignored is a little easier to forgive  once they actually get on the subway  after all you know what they say about  new york subway riders there's also the  grand central station fight in john wick  chapter 3 parabellum where zero and his  henchmen go after jon as crowds of  passersby go about their business and as  bodies drop left and right no one bats  an eye yes new yorkers generally like to  keep to themselves but frankly this is  ridiculous john wick is a fearsome  killing machine known for his ability to  take out entire squads of combatants on  his own according to rotten tomatoes his  body count throughout chapters 1-3 adds  up to a whopping 299 and that's just  what we see on screen  so why does everyone seem to like him so  much it's not just the code that seems  to keep people from messing with wick  once he's retired and settled down  everywhere he goes in the first film he  commands respect sharon the concierge of  the continental and winston both seem  very fond of him harry another assassin  helps him out which costs him his life  aurelio clearly has deep respect for him  in the sequels the bowery king also  seems to give wick a lot of leeway  despite their past interactions being  less than constructive is it the dogs  that was played as a dark joke at times  wick's return to the life is fueled by  the theft of his car and the death of  his dog which stings particularly bad  since the dog was a posthumous gift from  his late wife helen but this is john  wick baba yaga a man who once killed  three people with a pencil by all  accounts he's killed more people than  freddy krueger and jason voorhees  complained he's pretty damn scary if  he's coming after you and you probably  wouldn't be inclined to greet him with a  smile but he likes dogs so that makes  him a heck of a guy  another questionable thing wic fans  ignore is how often wick's opponents  will give him a moment to compose  himself before they continue fighting to  the death the best example of this is a  final boss fight for the zero and his  henchmen in parabellum john manages to  escape to the continental after being  chased by zero and his men and he  appears to be safe however winston  defies the high table and the  continental is deconsecrated meaning  once forbidden activities are now  allowed on the grounds zero's martial  artists henchmen fight with john in the  continental they are fresh for fighting  while jon is tired from all the  relentless attacks he survives so far  they have a clear advantage over him  several times yet they continuously stop  the fight to give john a chance to  compose himself ostensibly as a sign of  honor they have a job to do but they're  apparently so thrilled to fight the  legendary john wick that they wind up  losing instead in most other films jon  would have been dead several times in  that fight and in many of the others he  gets into as well but in the john wick  world like in a child's game of tag  timeouts are a natural part of combat  there's nothing like a good fight scene  on motorcycles but anyone who knows  anything about bikes can't help but  scoff at moments like when john flips  one cycle to take out another it's a  cool looking stunt but it also defies  the laws of physics when you look at the  behind the scenes of stunts such as the  motorcycle chasers in the third film the  use of cgi is made quite apparent  similarly wic can fall off the roof of a  skyscraper and survive thanks to the  magic of computers as well as the  stunned men who get paid to do the  dangerous work keanu reeves doesn't do  himself series director chad stahelski  is a former stuntman himself so he knows  full well what is physically possible  and what isn't in a world as large and  outrageous as that of john wick sahelsky  knows that only the biggest and most  outlandish stunts will suffice so maybe  a motorcycle wouldn't fly backwards but  would instead slide off to the side but  it sure does look cooler when it happens  in the movies  sure dunwick takes place in a highly  stylized fictional world where anything  goes but as its scale grows across  borders and oceans it becomes  increasingly difficult to believe that  the machinations of the high table have  gone completely unnoticed and then  checked by outsiders the films make it  clear that at least one police officer  knows who john wick is a trope not  uncommon for mob movies but there is no  sense of exactly what an average  bystander believes eunan john  evening jimmy  noise complain  noise complaint  john wick features gruesome kills in  public spaces huge explosions and even  that one moment where wick rides a horse  through the city so if everyone's trying  to stay totally unseen they're not doing  a very good job the franchise posits  that there is a code among the assassins  dictating that no bystanders are to be  harmed but there must be collateral  damage at some point which would then  come with cops investigations and once  the truth is discovered worldwide  headlines jimmy the police officer who  knows jon is presumably on the payroll  so is everyone else in the world as well  is anyone glimpsed on screen truly  innocent it's hard to tell gastly  yeah gas leak  joseph tarasava is portrayed by alfie  allen as an indolent spoiled brat he's  entitled arrogant and unfortunately for  him not very bright but seriously how  does he not know who john wick is once  our elio realizes the car joseph has  brought to his chop shop belongs to wick  he rats him out to his father viggo the  head of the tarasov crime family vigo  has a talk with his insubordinate son  explaining that john wick is more than  just some assassin he's the most feared  enforcer of all and he was once on  vigo's payroll josef in all of his  entitlement thinks he can just take out  jon himself but he has no idea of the  wrath about to come his way the thing is  everyone in the wick world knows who  john wick is they know the gruesome  stories they know his nicknames they  know he got out of the business for love  how does joseph the son of wick's former  boss not to recognize the man he took  everything from even after jon spoke the  same russian dialect to him yosef's  clearly a major part of his father's  business even if he's not the best  employee in the organization yes joseph  is a dope but it seems odd that he had  never even heard of the man who killed  all of his father's enemies in a single  bloody night  the john wick franchise has filled with  impossibilities but one of the more  questionable ones involves jon's long  trek through the desert in john wick  chapter three parabellum after being  declared excommunicado and finding  bharada the master of coin sophia's  former boss who is in charge of the coin  making jon learns that he cannot find  the high table but rather that they must  come to him he is told to walk and walk  until he can walk no more and if he's  deemed worthy the high table will scoop  him up and allow him to speak to the  elder so john walks alone for days  without water and collapses he should be  dead there is nothing around him for  miles yet the high table finds him  easily and picks him up how does a high  table locate wick do they have invisible  drones exceptionally powerful binoculars  did they somehow hide a tracker on him  for that matter how does a high table  function at all there are obviously  switchboard operators the elder and the  adjudicator but how do they keep  everyone in line all of these are  questions that may never be answered  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and to  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

